-- title:
--   From HTo G Of GHat Facts And Half Sandwich
-- statement:
--   **G-hat facts and repeated half-sandwich estimates yield the from-H-to-G comparison.**
--
--   Let $\psi_{bi}$ be a normalized bipartite state, let $S$ be a successor strategy, and let $F$ be an indexed polynomial family. Let $\gamma,\zeta\ge0$ with $\zeta\le1$. Assume the G-hat facts package, namely that the completed G-hat left and right families are $\operatorname{SDDRel}$-related under the uniform slice-question distribution with error `gHatSelfConsistencyError(\zeta)`, and that the completed G-hat pair products are $\operatorname{SDDOpRel}$-related under the uniform slice-pair distribution with error `gHatCommutationError(params,\gamma,\zeta)`. Also assume that for every natural number $j\ge2$, the corresponding repeated G-hat half-sandwich families are $\operatorname{SDDOpRel}$-related under the uniform distribution on $j$-tuples of points, with error `commuteGHalfSandwichError(params,\gamma,\zeta,j)`. For any $k\in\mathbb N$, these hypotheses imply the scalar `FromHToGStatement`, namely
--
--   $$
--   \left|M_{\mathrm{all}}(S,\psi_{bi},F,k)-T_{\mathrm{tail}}(\psi_{bi},F,k)\right|
--   \le E_{H\to G},
--   $$
--
--   where
--
--   $$
--   E_{H\to G}=46k^2m\left(\gamma^{1/32}+\zeta^{1/32}+(d/q)^{1/32}\right).
--   $$
--
--   This is the internal comparison theorem used by both the strategy-state wrapper and the commutativity-based completeness route.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToG_ofGHatFactsAndHalfSandwich`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
